# Line endings.
#
# The project is built on Linux (CI matrix, MSYS2, the headless plugin jobs) and
# on Windows.  One convention for both: LF in the repository and LF in the
# working tree.  Without this file the convention is per-file folklore, and a
# single editor or code-generating tool re-flips a file and turns a 40-line
# change into a 1500-line one.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Batch files are the one exception.  cmd.exe parses labels and `goto` on its
# own line-ending rules and mis-handles a bare LF, so these stay CRLF in the
# working tree.  `eol=crlf` converts on checkout and normalizes back to LF in
# the index, so the repository stays consistent.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never normalized, never treated as text by diff or merge.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.tif   binary
*.tiff  binary
*.bmp   binary
*.iwi   binary
*.hdr   binary
*.ico   binary
*.obj   binary
*.lib   binary
